    "title": "Bode Plot",
    "field": "Electronics / Electrical Engineering",
    "plotType": "Dual semi-log line plot (magnitude in dB and phase in degrees vs. log frequency)",
    "description": "A Bode plot shows how a circuit or system responds across frequency, using two stacked graphs: gain in decibels on top and phase shift in degrees below, both against a logarithmic frequency axis. The magnitude curve is flat in the passband and then rolls off along straight-line asymptotes at each pole or zero, while the phase sweeps between characteristic plateaus. Engineers rely on it because the log axes turn multiplicative filter stages into simple additive slopes you can sketch and stack by hand.",
