    "whatItTellsYou": "The flat region marks the passband gain, the -3 dB point marks the cutoff (bandwidth), and each -20 dB/decade drop in slope signals one more pole. Reading phase near the gain-crossover gives the phase margin, so a shrinking margin warns you the feedback loop is heading toward instability.",
